abstract:
  A read-only, passive scanner that checks a REDCap host for exposure
  to and compromise by CVE-2026-90817, the unauthenticated survey-endpoint
  remote-code-execution vulnerability abused by the XMRig cryptomining
  campaign. It compares the installed REDCap version against the patched
  releases and hunts the documented indicators of compromise (web shell,
  miner staging, masquerading processes, local miner API, attacker-IP
  connections, cron/SSH/profile persistence, and anti-forensics) without
  sending any HTTP requests or reproducing the exploit. It distinguishes
  the DataImportController-via-survey-passthru attack hallmark from
  legitimate REDCap traffic and correlates attack timestamps in the
  web-server logs against the mitigation date to judge compromise
  likelihood.
